<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the notarized PhotoBlaze.app.

  Intentionally EMPTY: PhotoBlaze is a non-sandboxed Developer ID app that needs no
  hardened-runtime exceptions. Unlike an Electron app (V8 JIT), a Rust binary is AOT —
  no `allow-jit` / `allow-unsigned-executable-memory`. It loads only Apple-signed system
  frameworks (Metal, AppKit, ImageIO), so no `disable-library-validation`. It makes no
  in-process network calls (the About link opens in the user's browser via the OS), so no
  `network.client`. The hardened runtime itself is enabled by `codesign --options runtime`
  in scripts/release-macos.sh; adding needless exceptions would only weaken it.
-->
